  ("At what age should a Stoney Creek furnace be replaced?", "With a tune-up every year, a gas furnace commonly gives you 15 to 20 years of service. Past 20 years, parts get harder to find and efficiency lags well behind a new 96% AFUE model, so a replacement quote is worth having."),
  ("Will the ductwork in my Stoney Creek house work with a new heat pump?", "Usually, yes. A central heat pump connects to the same ducts as your AC, but we test static pressure and return air first, since undersized ducts are the main reason a heat pump underperforms."),
  ("Do I save anything by replacing the furnace and AC in one job?", "If both are over 15 years old, replacing them together is often cheaper than two separate jobs. The indoor coil and outdoor unit also need to match, so doing them together avoids a mismatched system."),
  ("How is furnace installation in Stoney Creek priced?", "A new high-efficiency furnace runs from $3,300 installed, while a cold-climate heat pump on your existing ducts starts at $5,500. Installed pricing depends on size and installation requirements, such as duct or panel changes, and we lock the number in writing."),
